From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DockSeed <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 15:45:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: a733: offer the DSU cluster OFF idle state

Add cluster-sleep-0, PSCI power level 1 (arm,psci-suspend-param
0x01010000: power-down, level 1, StateID 0), and list it after the
core-level state in every cpu@N's cpu-idle-states. There is one DSU
cluster, so there is one state for all eight cores; with the original
PSCI idle binding the firmware coordinates, and the cluster goes down
only when all eight cores have asked for it.

Needs the boot chain's allwinner-a733-dsu-cluster-off-state (the DSU PPU
policy floor at OFF, level 1 accepted, the GIC-600 redistributor powered
down around the cluster power-down). A firmware without it refuses
0x01010000 with INVALID_PARAMETERS, and Linux's PSCI cpuidle driver then
fails that state.

The vendor device tree offers the same state with its own latencies;
they are not used. Ours are measured on the 8 GiB board at the lowest OPP
(247 MHz on both clusters, the worst case), with a timer wake on one A55
and one A76 while every other core idles in this state, 6000 wakes per
core (3000 on the first), on two boot chains (with and without PSCI_STAT):
- entry-latency-us 100: the wake latency reaches its plateau once the
  timer fires 100 us or more after the last core went idle (before that
  the cluster is still going down, and the wake is shorter).
- exit-latency-us 510: the largest wake from the fully entered state
  (d >= 100 us), 505 us, rounded up; p50 284-294, p99 294-306 us. Wakes
  late by whole 4 ms ticks (0.3 %) are left out: the same run with the
  core state instead shows them at the same rate, so they belong to the
  timer path, not to this state.
- entry + exit = 610 us bounds every wake seen while the cluster was
  going down (worst 534 us from the last core's entry).
- min-residency-us 10000 is not an energy measurement: the wall meter
  resolves no power difference between this state offered and not, so no
  break-even could be measured. It stays above both floors that are
  known: the core state's 3570 and entry + exit.

Assisted-by: Claude
---
 .../sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s-minimal.dts         | 39 +++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 31 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s-minimal.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s-minimal.dts
index dd668bc..a0d6c2d 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s-minimal.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s-minimal.dts
@@ -91,7 +91,7 @@ cpu0: cpu@0 {
 			i-cache-line-size = <64>;
 			i-cache-sets = <128>;
 			next-level-cache = <&L2_0>;
-			cpu-idle-states = <&cpu_sleep_0_a55>;
+			cpu-idle-states = <&cpu_sleep_0_a55 &cluster_sleep_0>;
 		};
 
 		cpu1: cpu@100 {
@@ -108,7 +108,7 @@ cpu1: cpu@100 {
 			i-cache-line-size = <64>;
 			i-cache-sets = <128>;
 			next-level-cache = <&L2_1>;
-			cpu-idle-states = <&cpu_sleep_0_a55>;
+			cpu-idle-states = <&cpu_sleep_0_a55 &cluster_sleep_0>;
 		};
 
 		cpu2: cpu@200 {
@@ -125,7 +125,7 @@ cpu2: cpu@200 {
 			i-cache-line-size = <64>;
 			i-cache-sets = <128>;
 			next-level-cache = <&L2_2>;
-			cpu-idle-states = <&cpu_sleep_0_a55>;
+			cpu-idle-states = <&cpu_sleep_0_a55 &cluster_sleep_0>;
 		};
 
 		cpu3: cpu@300 {
@@ -142,7 +142,7 @@ cpu3: cpu@300 {
 			i-cache-line-size = <64>;
 			i-cache-sets = <128>;
 			next-level-cache = <&L2_3>;
-			cpu-idle-states = <&cpu_sleep_0_a55>;
+			cpu-idle-states = <&cpu_sleep_0_a55 &cluster_sleep_0>;
 		};
 
 		cpu4: cpu@400 {
@@ -159,7 +159,7 @@ cpu4: cpu@400 {
 			i-cache-line-size = <64>;
 			i-cache-sets = <128>;
 			next-level-cache = <&L2_4>;
-			cpu-idle-states = <&cpu_sleep_0_a55>;
+			cpu-idle-states = <&cpu_sleep_0_a55 &cluster_sleep_0>;
 		};
 
 		cpu5: cpu@500 {
@@ -176,7 +176,7 @@ cpu5: cpu@500 {
 			i-cache-line-size = <64>;
 			i-cache-sets = <128>;
 			next-level-cache = <&L2_5>;
-			cpu-idle-states = <&cpu_sleep_0_a55>;
+			cpu-idle-states = <&cpu_sleep_0_a55 &cluster_sleep_0>;
 		};
 
 		/*
@@ -210,7 +210,7 @@ cpu6: cpu@600 {
 			i-cache-line-size = <64>;
 			i-cache-sets = <256>;
 			next-level-cache = <&L2_6>;
-			cpu-idle-states = <&cpu_sleep_0_a76>;
+			cpu-idle-states = <&cpu_sleep_0_a76 &cluster_sleep_0>;
 		};
 
 		cpu7: cpu@700 {
@@ -227,7 +227,7 @@ cpu7: cpu@700 {
 			i-cache-line-size = <64>;
 			i-cache-sets = <256>;
 			next-level-cache = <&L2_7>;
-			cpu-idle-states = <&cpu_sleep_0_a76>;
+			cpu-idle-states = <&cpu_sleep_0_a76 &cluster_sleep_0>;
 		};
 
 		cpu-map {
@@ -284,6 +284,29 @@ cpu_sleep_0_a76: cpu-sleep-0-a76 {
 				min-residency-us = <3570>;
 				arm,psci-suspend-param = <0x00010000>;
 			};
+
+			/*
+			 * DSU cluster OFF (PSCI power level 1), one state
+			 * for the one DSU cluster, offered after the core state
+			 * on all eight cores. PSCI coordinates: the cluster goes
+			 * down only when all eight cores ask for it, and the DSU
+			 * cleans the L3 on the way (BL31
+			 * allwinner-a733-dsu-cluster-off-state). Latencies
+			 * measured at the lowest OPP with timer wakes on an
+			 * A55 and an A76: the cluster is down 100 us
+			 * after the last core went idle, and the largest wake
+			 * from it took 505 us. min-residency-us is not an
+			 * energy measurement; it stays above the core state's
+			 * and above entry + exit.
+			 */
+			cluster_sleep_0: cluster-sleep-0 {
+				compatible = "arm,idle-state";
+				local-timer-stop;
+				entry-latency-us = <100>;
+				exit-latency-us = <510>;
+				min-residency-us = <10000>;
+				arm,psci-suspend-param = <0x01010000>;
+			};
 		};
 	};
 
